From b2f60ca76243ec719b0dde883dc5e7c794935e2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mining: serve compact templates and mined-header submission
 from snapshots

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics. The candidate repair below
changes this boundary and requires new validation evidence.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add SnapshotPublisher RCU snapshots for lock-free read RPCs and O(1)
getblocktemplate / submitminedheader.

Original-Commit: 399c3d5cf2aa9602aff967024c7f4053b06d206c
Original-Patch: ecash/014
Split-Concern: mining-rpc

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Complete the mining RPC owner against repaired coroutine and immutable-snapshot prerequisites. Select only pinned entries, retain overlay all-fit and custom ready-heap selection, share synchronized lazy mining caches across metadata-only generations, and preserve bounded template history. Capture actual ABC tip-dependent miner-fund/staking activation, block version and CTOR ordering. Validate each cold template against actual parent coins/scripts before warm reuse; certify cached Merkle branches only for unique non-coinbase lists. Retain original assertions and add historical-generation, warm-lock-independence, invalid-P2SH and duplicate-Merkle regressions. Exclude unrelated GenerateBlock root skipping and explicit default assembler options, which bypassed configured preconsensus mining. Native and functional evidence is archived; clean replay and all gates remain required.

